# Prometheus 3.13.1
# Version read from prometheus_build_info.
#
# Captured 2026-08-02 from a real Prometheus 3.13.1 configured to exercise every
# subsystem the rules read: two scrape jobs (one deliberately unresolvable), the
# repo's own prometheus.rules.yml and prometheus.records.yml loaded, an
# Alertmanager declared but unreachable, and a remote_write queue pointed at an
# unresolvable sink. Without that config a bare Prometheus emits none of the
# rule_*, notifications_*, target_* or remote_storage queue families.
#
# prometheus_remote_storage_samples_dropped_total is absent from this capture,
# and that is NOT a removal. It is a CounterVec labelled by `reason` with no
# child series pre-initialised, so it emits nothing until a sample is actually
# dropped. The remote_write sink here is unresolvable, which produces send
# failures, not drops -- nothing was relabelled away, too old, or an unknown
# ref. The declaration is byte-identical in v2.55.0 and v3.13.1
# (storage/remote/queue_manager.go, NewCounterVec with []string{"reason"}), and
# 3.13.1 still increments it in four code paths.
#
# alertmanager_* metrics are absent by nature: they belong to Alertmanager, not
# Prometheus, and this repo has no Alertmanager fixture. Three rules read them
# and they are present in production.
